<title>AUSTRIA: Germany's Rexrodt says EMU treaty offers leeway.</title>
<headline>Germany's Rexrodt says EMU treaty offers leeway.</headline>
<dateline>SALZBURG, Austria 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Economy Minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Saturday the Maastricht treaty on Europe's single currency offered some leeway for countries attempting to meet the three percent budget deficit criterium.</p>
<p>&quot;There is leeway but not much leeway,&quot; Rexrodt told reporters after meeting his Austrian and Swiss counterparts in this Alpine city.</p>
</text>
